ue in the United States of America.</article-title><source>Public Health Monographs</source><volume>26</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>120</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004813-VanErt1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van Ert</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name><name><surname>Easterday</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Huynh</surname><given-names>LY</given-names></name><name><surname>Okinaka</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><name><surname>Hugh-Jones</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Global genetic population structure of Bacillus anthracis.</article-title><source>PLoS ONE</source><volume>2</volume><fpage>e461</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17520020</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004813-Pearson1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pearson</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Busch</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Ravel</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Read</surname><given-names>TD</given-names></name><name><surname>Rhoton</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Phylogenetic discovery bias in Bacillus anthracis using single-nucleotide polymorphisms from whole-genome sequencing.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>101</volume><fpage>13536</fpage><lpage>13541</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15347815</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004813-Dragon1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dragon</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Bader</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitchell</surname><given-names>J</given-names><